  {
    "pkheadingid": 515,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 554,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70099,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 117,
        "headingId": 554,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em> intratubular germ cell elements with appropriate histological patterns.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> immunohistochemical confirmation with appropriate markers.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-04-15T14:52:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 513,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 552,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70100,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 117,
        "headingId": 552,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Intratubular disease is by definition in&nbsp;situ (Tis), but it is almost inevitably associated with invasive disease.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T11:26:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 514,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 553,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70101,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 117,
        "headingId": 553,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Nearly all examples are associated with invasive germ cell neoplasms, on which the prognosis and prediction should be based.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T11:26:13"
      }
    ],
